        "why": "The section is named by what it holds, so the drawing is built by counting: nine doublets on the outside, two singlets in the middle, and every other label hangs on one of those eleven tubules.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing nine single tubules. Each peripheral unit is a DOUBLET of two tubules.",
          "Drawing the two central tubules joined as a doublet. They are two separate singlets.",
          "Drawing the 9 + 0 pattern. That is a centriole or a basal body, not a flagellum."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Nine outside in pairs, two inside alone: 9 + 2. A centriole is 9 + 0.",
        "margin_note": "Count the nine doublets before you label anything. Eight or ten loses the mark."
